{% comment %}
  Font declarations, shared by every layout.

  Usage:
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true %}        <- declares faces, applies Arial
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true, family: "'Hanken Grotesk', Arial, sans-serif" %}

  The faces are always declared; a browser only downloads a font something
  actually uses, so declaring on a layout that does not apply them costs
  nothing. `family` chooses what the applying rules set, which is how Hanken
  Grotesk is live on layout/suf.liquid while layout/theme.liquid stays on
  Arial.

  THEME.LIQUID STAYS ON ARIAL. SETTLED, not pending. Decided 2026-08-30.

  This was once phrased as "until the legacy templates have been reviewed",
  which read as a task someone would finish. Nobody will. The Indivisible
  faces have been corrupt for years (see below), so those ~30 templates have
  rendered in Arial for their whole life -- that IS what the legacy site looks
  like, and restyling every one of them to make a font consistent is work
  spent on pages the redesign is replacing.

  The direction is to migrate templates onto layout/suf.liquid, where Hanken
  Grotesk already applies, and let this shrink. Do not "fix" it by passing a
  family here.

  ONE EXCEPTION, and it is deliberate: sections/suf-nav.liquid opts back into
  Hanken Grotesk for itself. It is the same section on both layouts and has to
  look identical on both. See the font block in _suf-nav.scss.

  The applying rules carry !important because both layouts load
  dt-framework.css, which sets font-family on the same elements at higher
  specificity.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY NOT INDIVISIBLE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  All four Indivisible files -- both .woff and both .woff2, in this repo AND in
  the live theme, byte-identical -- were destroyed by a UTF-8 text round trip.
  Every byte >= 0x80 became U+FFFD (EF BF BD), inflating each file ~75% past
  the length its own header declares. A structural decode finds 0 of 15 WOFF
  tables readable: tags read "=o?=" and "Nloc" rather than "cmap" and "glyf".
  No browser can parse them, and the substitution is lossy, so they cannot be
  repaired. The site rendered in Arial for years as a result.

  Hanken Grotesk replaces it: OFL-licensed, self-hosted, 400/600/700/800/900,
  woff2, latin subset, ~68 KB for the five. Self-hosted rather than linked
  from Google's CDN -- two fewer origins on the critical path, and Google Fonts
  sends visitor IPs to Google. See docs/migration.md.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY 800 IS A REAL FACE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The design asks for font-weight 800 in ~50 places -- every heading, figure,
  eyebrow and label. With only a 700 face declared, a browser has two bad
  options and takes both depending on the engine: render 700 and ignore the
  difference, or synthesise a faux-bold by smearing the 700 outlines. Neither
  is the typeface's own 800, and the smeared version is visibly worse at
  display sizes, which is exactly where this design uses it.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DECLARING A FACE IS FREE; PRELOADING ONE IS NOT
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  All five faces are declared here unconditionally. @font-face is lazy: the
  browser downloads a file only when something on the page actually computes
  to that family AND weight, so declaring a weight no page uses costs five
  lines of CSS and zero bytes.

  `preload_tag` in the layout is the opposite -- it fetches at high priority
  before the browser knows whether anything needs it. Only the weights that
  paint on first load belong there. See layout/suf.liquid for which two, and
  why the other three are deliberately left to load on demand.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  set_weights
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The applying rules set a font-weight as well as a family, to normalise the
  legacy templates. That is wrong for layout/suf.liquid: `h1, h2, ...` is
  (0,0,1), the suf base layer is `:where(.suf-body) h1` which is ALSO (0,0,1)
  because :where() contributes nothing, and this snippet renders AFTER
  suf.css -- so the tie went to whichever came last, and every suf heading was
  rendering at 700 while the stylesheet asked for 800.

  Pass `set_weights: false` on a layout that supplies its own weights. The
  family rules keep their !important; those are still doing real work.

  Both files were verified before being committed: signature wOF2, declared
  length equal to actual byte length, zero U+FFFD sequences. Do that check on
  any font added here.

  Licence: SIL OFL 1.1, see OFL.txt in the repo root. The OFL requires the
  licence text to travel with the font, so keep them together.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign family = family | default: 'Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif' -%}
{%- if set_weights == nil -%}{%- assign set_weights = true -%}{%- endif -%}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-400.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-600.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-700.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-800.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-900.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  {%- if apply -%}
    p, blockquote, li, a, body, footer, aside, nav, section, article, div, span,
    input, button, textarea, label {
      font-family: {{ family }} !important;
      {%- if set_weights %}
      font-weight: 400;
      {%- endif %}
    }
    h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, strong, b, th {
      font-family: {{ family }} !important;
      {%- if set_weights %}
      font-weight: 700;
      {%- endif %}
    }
  {%- endif -%}
</style>
